       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Ibuprofen 4000 mg four times daily comes to 16,000 mg/day. The usual maximum is 3,200 mg/day for outpatients and 2,400 mg/day in most inpatient settings, so this is 5\u20136 times the ceiling. At that level the risks include severe GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, and CNS toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), which may be a decimal or extra-zero slip\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 4000 mg per dose is what you intend, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy before it's entered."
